card.statement:
Let $I \subseteq R$ and $\Delta \subseteq \Sigma$ be such that $P_{\Delta}(v)e_{k\ell}(\tau_{r}^\star(\sigma)(x+\tau_{r}(z))$ and $P_{\Delta}(x)e_{k\ell}(\sigma(x+z))$ are smooth functions. Then:

$$\mathcal{D}_{I}^{v}\left(P_{\Delta}(v)e_{k\ell}(\tau_{r}^\star(\sigma)(x+\tau_{r}(z)))\right)=
\begin{cases}
\mathcal{D}_{I}^{v}\left(P_{\Delta}(x)e_{k\ell}(\sigma(x+z))\right), & \text{ if }\ \  (R_{\Delta})_{r}=I_{r}\\
-\mathcal{D}_{I}^{v}\left(P_{\Delta}(x)e_{k\ell}(\sigma(x+z))\right), & \text{ if }\ \  (R_{\Delta})_{r}\neq I_{r}
\end{cases}$$
